# Template: Front-End Error Recovery

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file provides a specialized template for error recovery requirements in front-end development for the PolygonExpress project. It focuses solely on giving structure to the initial requirements.md file for features that need robust error handling.

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file is a Manual rule type and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in the plan-mode message-command:

```
plan-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/plan-mode/template-error-recovery.mdc
```

## Requirements Template

When this template is applied, it will create the following structure in requirements.md:

```markdown
# Error-Resilient Feature Requirements

## Objective
[What is the purpose of this feature?]

## Functional Requirements
[What functionality should this feature provide?]

## Error Scenarios
[What error conditions need to be handled?]

Critical error scenarios:
- [Error scenario 1]: [Description and impact]
- [Error scenario 2]: [Description and impact]
- [Error scenario 3]: [Description and impact]

## Recovery Requirements
[How should the feature recover from each error scenario?]

## User Feedback Requirements
[What information should be presented to users during error conditions?]

## Graceful Degradation
[How should the feature degrade when recovery isn't possible?]

## Fallback UI States
[What alternative UI states should be shown during error conditions?]

## Error Logging Requirements
[What error information should be logged for debugging?]

## Success Criteria
[How will we know errors are being handled correctly?]

## Testing Requirements
[What specific error scenarios must be tested?]
```

## Template Application

When the template is applied, I will:
1. Create or update requirements.md with this template
2. Leave all sections empty for completion
3. Wait for the requirements to be completed before proceeding with any planning

## Next Steps
1. Complete the requirements template with error handling details
2. Once requirements are complete, proceed with planning the implementation approach

## Use Cases
- API-dependent features
- Critical user workflows
- Payment processing components
- Data submission forms
- Authentication features
